IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `laa-compensation`

-- Land Acquisition Act 1966, ss 33, 34 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_laa.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a shophouse valued at current zoning` MEANS Valuation WITH
    `market value at current zoning` IS 2000000
    `value with hope of rezoning` IS 3500000
    `value declared for tax within 2 years` IS 0
    `there is such a tax declaration` IS FALSE
    `uplift from unlawful use` IS 0

`a shophouse the owner under-declared for duty last year` MEANS Valuation WITH
    `market value at current zoning` IS 2000000
    `value with hope of rezoning` IS 3500000
    `value declared for tax within 2 years` IS 1600000
    `there is such a tax declaration` IS TRUE
    `uplift from unlawful use` IS 0

`a house with an illegal extra storey` MEANS Valuation WITH
    `market value at current zoning` IS 2000000
    `value with hope of rezoning` IS 2000000
    `value declared for tax within 2 years` IS 0
    `there is such a tax declaration` IS FALSE
    `uplift from unlawful use` IS 300000

`a house declared above market for tax` MEANS Valuation WITH
    `market value at current zoning` IS 2000000
    `value with hope of rezoning` IS 2000000
    `value declared for tax within 2 years` IS 2500000
    `there is such a tax declaration` IS TRUE
    `uplift from unlawful use` IS 0

`a plain acquisition` MEANS Claim WITH
    `market value allowed` IS 1000000
    `severance damage` IS 0
    `injurious affection` IS 0
    `betterment to other land` IS 0
    `relocation expenses` IS 20000
    `title costs` IS 5000

`a severance with partial betterment` MEANS Claim WITH
    `market value allowed` IS 1000000
    `severance damage` IS 100000
    `injurious affection` IS 0
    `betterment to other land` IS 40000
    `relocation expenses` IS 0
    `title costs` IS 0

`a betterment larger than the damage` MEANS Claim WITH
    `market value allowed` IS 1000000
    `severance damage` IS 50000
    `injurious affection` IS 0
    `betterment to other land` IS 200000
    `relocation expenses` IS 20000
    `title costs` IS 0

§ `s 33(1)(a)`

#ASSERT `the valuation date` 4 TRUE EQUALS "the date of the section 3 notification"
#ASSERT `the valuation date` 8 TRUE EQUALS "the date of the section 5 declaration"
#ASSERT `the valuation date` 0 FALSE EQUALS "the date of the section 5 declaration"

§ `s 33(5)`

#ASSERT `the market value allowed` `a shophouse valued at current zoning` EQUALS 2000000
#ASSERT `the market value allowed` `a shophouse the owner under-declared for duty last year` EQUALS 1600000
#ASSERT `the market value allowed` `a house with an illegal extra storey` EQUALS 1700000
#ASSERT `the market value allowed` `a house declared above market for tax` EQUALS 2000000

§ `s 33(1), (2)`

#ASSERT `the compensation` `a plain acquisition` EQUALS 1025000
#ASSERT `the compensation` `a severance with partial betterment` EQUALS 1060000
#ASSERT `the compensation` `a betterment larger than the damage` EQUALS 1020000

§ `s 34`

#ASSERT NOT `the Board may take the matter into account` `the owner's reluctance to sell`
#ASSERT NOT `the Board may take the matter into account` `the urgency of the project`
#ASSERT NOT `the Board may take the matter into account` `the value the project will add to the acquired land`
#ASSERT NOT `the Board may take the matter into account` `a renovation done after the notification`
#ASSERT `the Board may take the matter into account` `a repair after the notification approved by the Commissioner of Lands`
#ASSERT `the Board may take the matter into account` `a comparable sale proved bona fide by the appellant`
#ASSERT NOT `the Board may take the matter into account` `a comparable sale not proved bona fide`

